Different sets of correlation functions were generated as a function of \(\rm p_{T}\) and \(\rm\langle N_{ch}\rangle\) to allow a comparison of \(\rm v_{1}^{even}\) and \(\rm v_{3}\) (for each collision system) for different dimensionless sizes (\(\rm RT\propto\langle N_{ch}^{1/3}\rangle\)) and eccentricities.

