Figures 5.13 and 5.14 show the two- and four-particle elliptic flow and their ratios, vs. centrality for identified particles in U+U (\(\sqrt{\rm s_{\rm NN}}=193\) GeV) and Cu+Au collisions (\(\sqrt{\rm s_{\rm NN}}=200\) GeV) respectively. The mass ordering effect on the magnitude of two- and four-particle elliptic flow can be seen in panels (a, b and c). This effect, which cancels for the ratio \(\rm v_{2}\{4\}/\rm v_{2}\{2\}\), shows the expected decrease in the magnitude from central to peripheral collisions, consistent with patterns expected when initial-state eccentricity fluctuations dominate.

